or drive up the market price. Short sellers and others, some of whom post anonymously on social media, may be positioned to profit if
our shares declines or otherwise exhibits volatility, and their activities can negatively affect our share price and increase the volatility
of our share price. These broad market and industry factors may seriously harm the market price of our Class B Subordinate Voting Shares,
regardless of our operating performance.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Following
